  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 122 PM CDT Wed Sep 2 2026\n\nThe main change today was the issuance of a Heat Advisory for \nthe southeast part of the forecast area (Stockton, KS to York, \nNE) for today through Friday. Afternoon heat index values may \napproach 105 degrees in some areas, and overnight lows will be \nnear record warmth (mid 70s). Rain chances remain very low \nthrough Thursday, although a rogue shower or storm cannot be \nruled out late tonight into Thursday morning (5% chance). \n\nThe heat potential for Saturday is a bit more uncertain, \nbecause a few showers/thunderstorms return to the forecast late \nFriday night. Lingering cloud cover COULD keep temperatures a \nbit cooler on Saturday, but if these don't materialize then it \nis possible that the Heat Advisory will be extended. \n\nLow chances for thunderstorms continue through the Holiday\nweekend as a series of upper disturbances are ejected from an\nupper low over the Pacific NW. Timing will generally favor the\novernight hours, but confidence in exact details remains low at\nthis range. The aforementioned upper low will weaken the upper\nridge that has been responsible for the recent round of heat.\nThis will result in slightly cooler (but still above-normal)\ntemperatures through the middle of next week.",
